## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/edgedetect.html
- Summary (EN): Finds edges in an image with several selectable algorithms. Does not cover the Edge Detect by Contour, Normal or Depth nodes.
- Résumé (FR) : Détecte les contours d'une image selon plusieurs méthodes : Sobel, Prewitt, Laplacien, simple ou Sobel seuillé.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: initial image to process (only input)"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source", "Mode: edges from Luminance, or Per Channel for RGB and RGBA inputs", "Method: Sobel, Prewitt, Laplacian, Simple or Thresholded Sobel", "Normalize: keeps output in 0 to 1", "Blur Before: blurs the image before detection", "High Threshold: strong-pixel cutoff, used only by Thresholded Sobel"]

- Caveats: ["High Threshold has no effect unless Method is Thresholded Sobel.", "Per Channel mode is meant for RGB and RGBA inputs.", "The page gives no default values or guidance on choosing a method."]

